WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.668
ROGER MARTINEZ:
Today we're talking

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:04.920
about VM Manager, Bare Metal
Solutions, and CloudSQL

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.787
Insights.

00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:08.370
I'm Roger Martinez, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.280
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.550
We've just announced VM Manager,
a suite of infrastructure

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.740
management tools designed
to simplify and automate

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.310
the maintenance of large
fleets of Compute Engine VMs.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.310
This Cloud native solution has
Google scale infrastructure

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.500
in mind, providing
a simplified toolset

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.110
for automated compliance
reporting and software

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.800
deployment at scale.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.070
Check out the blog
to learn more.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.100
Google is committed to being
a leader in open cloud.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.630
Part of that commitment
is Bare Metal Solution,

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.750
which enables developers
to run Oracle database

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.740
workloads on Google Cloud.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.060
And now we're announcing three
enhancements-- availability

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.230
in our 10th region, Montreal;
a new, smaller 8-core server;

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.680
and support for
PCI, DSS, and HIPAA.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.280
To learn more and see it in
action, head over to the blog.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.530
CloudSQL Insights is
a simple open tool

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.900
that helps developers quickly
understand and resolve

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.360
database performance
issues on CloudSQL,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.310
allowing your database
analysts to focus

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.650
on more strategic tasks.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.680
Even more helpful, we've made
insights for the previous seven

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.220
days available to everyone
at no additional cost.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.470
Those metrics will be
displayed in the dashboard,

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.720
so check them out for yourself.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.940
We've just announced
the general availability

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.750
of Dialogflow CX, part of
Google Cloud's contact center AI

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.990
solution, which includes a
brand-new set of capabilities

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.360
for advanced virtual agents.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.280
With this virtual
agent technology,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.710
your contact center agents
can focus on the highest

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.770
priority customer interactions
while your virtual agents

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.230
hold down the fort
handling routine calls.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.657
Check it out today.

00:01:41.657 --> 00:01:43.740
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.570
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:48.210
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.110
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.610
We'll see you in the Cloud.

